WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.728
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Worry vs. Real.

00:00:12.728 --> 00:00:17.456
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.456 --> 00:00:20.293
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.293 --> 00:00:23.130
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:31.640
Our minds hand us two kinds of thoughts, and they look almost the same.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:40.150
One kind is a real problem: something happening now, right in front of you.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:45.824
The other kind is a worry: a "what if" about later. It is not happening now.

00:00:45.824 --> 00:00:49.606
One question sorts them: is it happening now, in front of me? Let's practice.

00:00:49.606 --> 00:00:59.062
Pretend with me: a cup of water spills on the table. Splash. That is happening now.

00:00:59.062 --> 00:01:05.681
A real problem gets a next step. Fix the small part you can: wipe the water with a cloth.

00:01:05.681 --> 00:01:14.192
And if the spill is too big for you, tell a grown-up. Grown-ups are part of the plan.

00:01:14.192 --> 00:01:23.648
See the "now" door, open and bright? Real problems walk through it, one step at a time.

00:01:23.648 --> 00:01:34.049
Now the other kind. Pretend this thought: "What if it rains on our trip?"

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:39.723
Is it happening now? No. The sky is fine, and the trip is later. That is a worry.

00:01:39.723 --> 00:01:46.342
A worry gets parked kindly: say it — "I'm worried about rain" — then picture it resting in the worry box, for later.

00:01:46.342 --> 00:01:52.015
See the "later" door, gently closed? The worry waits there. It is not gone. It is just not now.

00:01:52.015 --> 00:01:58.635
Real problem: one next step. Worry: parked kindly, and back to now.

00:01:58.635 --> 00:02:06.199
And one rule for both kinds: if anything ever feels too big, tell a grown-up. Always.

00:02:06.199 --> 00:02:09.036
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:09.036 --> 00:02:12.818
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:12.818 --> 00:02:16.601
You're ready for what's next.
